# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
node_modules/
.env
.env.local

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Category 1: template ships empty, the clone populates.
#
# These folders hold per-instance OS state. The template repo has nothing to
# put in them, so they are ignored here to keep the public template clean.
#
# If you cloned this to run your own company, you almost certainly want your
# OS tracked in git. Delete this block after bootstrap so your identity,
# context, memory, connections, and roster are versioned like everything else.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
01-identity/
02-context/
04-memory/
05-connections/
06-agents/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Category 2: plain scratch. Never tracked, in the template or in a clone.
#
# .deliverables/ is local-only working scratch. It is NOT the deliverables
# folder. Only its README is tracked, and that README exists to say so.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.deliverables/*
!.deliverables/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored, and it should stay that way:
#
#   00-deliverables/   tracked work. Deliverables have to be reviewable,
#                      linkable from 00-tasks.md, and present in a fresh
#                      clone. That is the whole point of the folder.
#   00-tasks.md        the company-wide index over those deliverables.
#   00-templates/      reusable formats, shared across the company.
#   01-sops/           shipped framework: cross-agent conventions.
#   03-skills/         shipped framework: bootstrap-company, add-new-agent.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
